// Why: TLS trusts what the platform's certificate verifier says, so the
// verifier's refusals and its agreement with Go's must be checked.
// What: the blocks RT8-Cert-Verify and RT8-Cert-Roots for std/rt/cert.mk and
// each target's sys/cert.mk, with the test certificate CeDer.
// How: a self-signed certificate no store trusts, made once by a Go program
// (crypto/x509, P-256, CN "mk-rt8 test", DNS mk.test, serverAuth, valid 2000
// to 2200), refused with CERT_E_UNTRUSTEDROOT; bytes crypt32 cannot parse,
// and malformed records, refused before any chain is built; a cancelled
// scope's call. On Linux every call answers Unsupported. Run by the scheduler
// harness and by std/rt_deadline_test.go (its RT8- blocks).

